TITLE:: CompressorPanel
summary:: a compressor's controls as one view
categories:: Libraries>Compressor
related:: Classes/Compressor, Classes/CompressorGUI, Classes/CompressorCurveView, Classes/CompressorHistoryView, Classes/CompressorMeterView, Classes/ParaEQView

DESCRIPTION::
What every window that shows a compressor is built from: its own window
(link::Classes/CompressorGUI::), the master chain (FxChainPanel, which
ServerPanel opens), a SuperDirtGUI insert.

code::
 (o) COMPRESSOR   < glue          v >  save  ...
 +-------------------------------------+ +------------------+ +----------+
 | level · gain change listens to input v| | curve · down gain -4.0 dB| in gain out|
 |  the last 8 s, the threshold a line  | |  the transfer curve,     | |  #  #  # |
 |  through it and through the curve    | |  the dot the detector    | |  #  #  # |
 +-------------------------------------+ +------------------+ +----------+
 [dynamics][sidechain]
 | curve: mode threshold ratio knee range | | time: detector attack release lookahead | | output: makeup auto mix |
::

The frame every effect window shares - the header (power, the name, presets,
save, a menu with save as, delete, copy, paste and back to the defaults), the
display with its meters at the right, titled cards, the knobs and their
gestures, the output card last, the hint bar - and a compressor's face: the
history (link::Classes/CompressorHistoryView::) and the transfer curve
(link::Classes/CompressorCurveView::) on the meters' dB scale, with the
threshold one orchid line through both. Orchid, code::FxPalette.gain::, is
everything the compressor does to the level; blue is sound.

Two pages. strong::dynamics:: holds the curve card (mode, threshold and ratio
big, knee and range small - the four in orchid; the threshold's knob carries a
ring of where the detector is now) and the time card (detector, attack,
release, lookahead). strong::sidechain:: swaps the history for the sidechain eq
(a link::Classes/ParaEQView:: with the spectrum of what the detector listens to
behind it, see link::Classes/CompressorSidechainSource::) and the cards for
what it listens to (source, audition, link) and the eq's selected dot (its
number on the card's title line, flat, eq in/out, freq, gain, width or a cut's
res, slope). The curve, the meters and the output card (makeup, auto, mix) stay
on both. The sidechain tab wears a dot while the detector hears anything but
its own plain input: another source, the eq in, link under 100 %, audition.

What does nothing in the current settings is dimmed and its hint says why: at
1:1 the threshold, knee, range, attack and release; link with one channel;
makeup, auto and mix while auditioning; the eq's controls while it is out, the
gain of a cut, the slope of a band. Off, every control is muted but stays
editable.

code::
c = Compressor.new;
w = Window("a compressor", Rect(100, 100, 960, 520)).front;
p = CompressorPanel(c, w);
w.layout = VLayout(p.view);
p.running = true;         // meters, and the sidechain's spectrum while its page shows
p.page = 1;               // the sidechain page
w.onClose = { p.remove };
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
ARGUMENT:: comp
The link::Classes/Compressor:: to show, or nil for an empty panel.
ARGUMENT:: parent
A view to build in, or nil.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: comp
The compressor shown. Setting it re-points the header, both views, the meter,
the sidechain eq and its spectrum and every control; nil empties the panel.

METHOD:: view
The panel's link::Classes/View::.

METHOD:: page
Which page shows: 0 dynamics, 1 sidechain.

METHOD:: showEq
The sidechain page (true) or dynamics (false), as the old show eq button did.
ARGUMENT:: bool

METHOD:: running
While true the compressor reports its levels (code::comp.meter::) and, on the
sidechain page, the spectrum runs. A window sets it while the panel shows.

METHOD:: header
The panel's FxHeader.

METHOD:: curveView
The link::Classes/CompressorCurveView::.

METHOD:: historyView
The link::Classes/CompressorHistoryView::.

METHOD:: meterView
The link::Classes/CompressorMeterView::: an FxMeter with the gain bar.

METHOD:: eqView
The sidechain eq's link::Classes/ParaEQView::.

METHOD:: spectrum
The ParaEQSpectrum behind the sidechain eq.

METHOD:: tabs
The page switch (an FxSwitch).

METHOD:: selected
Which dot of the sidechain eq the card works on, 0 .. 6 (the five bands, then
the low and the high cut). The eq view owns it: set code::p.eqView.selected::.

METHOD:: knobs
The parameter knobs by name (code::\threshold::, code::\ratio:: ...).

METHOD:: widgets
Every control the panel draws, for a check or a picture.

METHOD:: hints
An FxHintBar the panel labels its controls in; the two views write to it themselves.

METHOD:: refresh
Redraw from the compressor.

METHOD:: isClosed
Whether the view has gone.

METHOD:: remove
Stops listening, frees the spectrum's analyser and turns the meter off. Call it
in the window's onClose.
